{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-qou-obstruction-reduction","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:qou-obstruction-reduction","kind":"theorem","title":"Conditional on the Wigner-axiom inputs: the obstruction is a single integer $\\chi_A$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-wigner-axiom","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-classical-limit-obstruction","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-qu-to-qou","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-three-euler-characteristics"],"cites":["references/yekutieli2010","references/brown-zhang-2008","references/feng-tsygan-1991","references/hadfield-krahmer-2005","references/weibel1994"],"tags":["obstruction","classical-limit","hochschild-cohomology","observability","frobenius-duality","euler-characteristic","kummer"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qou_obstruction_reduction","text":"qou-obstruction-reduction.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:qou-obstruction-reduction\"></a><p><strong>Conditional on <a href=\"#conj:wigner-axiom\" data-at=\"stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-construction\">the Wigner axiom</a>.</strong> Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with archimedean base curve <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M_0</code>. Take as hypotheses the following four inputs, which are the content of the <a href=\"#conj:wigner-axiom\" data-at=\"stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-construction\">Wigner axiom</a> for the <a href=\"#def:classical-limit-obstruction\" data-at=\"stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-construction\">classical limit obstruction</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Obs}(\\mathbf{C}, q \\to 1)</code>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>(twisted duality)</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\dim HH^i(\\mathcal{U}_q, \\mathrm{Ad}) = \\dim HH_{3-i}(\\mathcal{U}_q, {}_\\nu\\mathrm{Ad})</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0 \\le i \\le 3</code>, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nu</code> is the Nakayama automorphism;</li>\n<li><strong>(twisted rigidity)</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\dim HH_1(\\mathcal{U}_q, {}_\\nu\\mathrm{Ad}) = 1</code>;</li>\n<li><strong>(Kummer vanishing)</strong> the obstruction vanishes at Kummer level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> iff <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\mid \\kappa_0</code>, for an integer <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa_0</code>;</li>\n<li><strong>(trace)</strong> the trace pairing sends the class <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi_A</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">w(A)</code> to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa_0</code>, and the image <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi_1</code> of the obstruction class equals that trace.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Then:</p>\n<p><strong>(a)</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\dim HH^2 = 1</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi_1 = \\chi_A</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>(b)</strong> For every <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\ge 1</code>, the obstruction vanishes at Kummer level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> iff <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\mid \\chi_A</code>.</p>\n<p>The identification <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi_A = \\chi_{\\mathrm{eu}}(M_0) = 2 - 2g(M_0)</code> is not part of this statement; the proof discusses it.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/qou-obstruction-reduction.md","heading":"Theorem","number":"21.4.11","page":"b/thm-qou-obstruction-reduction","qa":{"counts":{"pass":92,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":84},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BringsSurface.qou_obstruction_reduction","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/qou_obstruction_reduction.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
